# Current theses

## Thesis T-small-local-core: Keep HINT local and explicit
Status: accepted
Based-on: user:2026-09-17 refactoring decision

### Guidance
Keep HINT as one Node.js CLI whose canonical data is path-scoped Markdown. Do
not add a database, daemon, model call, plugin vocabulary, network import, or
hidden compatibility engine.

### Rationale
The product exists to leave compact, inspectable evidence and guidance for a
later agent without requiring another service or ecosystem.

### Revisit when
A concrete user need cannot be met by the fixed H–I–N–T Markdown workflow.

## Thesis T-output-contract: Keep machine output isolated
Status: accepted
Based-on: decision:CLI v1 contract

### Guidance
Write requested Markdown or one JSON value to stdout. Put verdicts, warnings,
and NEXT on stderr in text mode. Exit 0 on success, 1 on validation/check/
conflict failure, and 2 on usage or unresolved address.

### Rationale
Agents must be able to consume output without advisory prose corrupting it.

## Thesis T-safe-storage: Preserve scope and concurrent work
Status: accepted
Based-on: decision:CLI v1 storage contract

### Guidance
Resolve real paths inside the selected project boundary. Serialize each
read-modify-write, re-read under the lock, enforce requested revisions, and
publish through same-directory atomic rename.

### Rationale
Lexical checks miss symlink escapes and atomic rename alone still permits two
writers to lose one another's changes.

